      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/walkerton_virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Walkerton was a colonial‑era river ferry town and the historic site of Fort Mattaponi.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/walkerton_virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In July 1862, Union cavalry clashed with local Home Guard at Walkerton's ferry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/walkerton_virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "March 2, 1864, Walkerton hosted the Battle of Walkerton during the Kilpatrick‑Dahlgren Raid.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
